      "note": "_pkcs12_decode_safe_contents assumes oid is safe for fixed-literal strcmp dispatch, but it never clears the buffer before bagId parsing or the later attribute read. On the staged witness, bagId bytes 06 01 F7 survive the bag_type gate via GNUTLS_BAG_UNKNOWN, and attribute bytes 06 02 2A F2 are then read into the same oid buffer before the KEY_ID_OID comparison. The saved MSAN trace ties the sink back to the oid stack allocation and reports the first uninitialized byte at offset 4 in the compare window. A correct fix zero-initializes oid before these reads or avoids fixed-literal strcmp on partially initialized storage.",
